<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
    PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy — Glass (app target)

    The app collects nothing, so NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes is empty and
    NSPrivacyTracking is false. That is not an aspiration: §2 forbids sign-in,
    accounts, remote APIs and personal data collection, and there is no
    analytics or attribution SDK in the project to contradict it.

    NSPrivacyTrackingDomains is empty because the app contacts exactly one
    host — huggingface.co, to fetch the optional model file the student asked
    for — and that request carries no identifier. It is a file download, not
    tracking, so it belongs in neither list.

    NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes lists the required-reason APIs Apple's static
    check will find in this binary. Only two categories appear anywhere in the
    tree; there are no file-timestamp, boot-time, keyboard or pasteboard APIs:

    - UserDefaults. Declared with both reasons because SharedDefaults.suite is
      the app-group suite when the entitlement resolves (1C8F.1, shared with
      the widget extension) and falls back to .standard when it does not
      (CA92.1). Both paths ship, so both are declared.

    - Disk space. LocalModelService.hasRoomOnDisk() reads
      volumeAvailableCapacityForImportantUsage before starting the model
      download. E174.1 is the "is there room to write this file" reason,
      which is exactly what that function asks.

    Keep this in step with the code. Adding an SDK, a crash reporter, or any
    new required-reason API means editing this file in the same change.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>1C8F.1</string>
				<string>CA92.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryDiskSpace</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>E174.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
